@page "/prototype-scope"

<PageTitle>Prototype Scope - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<PageHero Eyebrow="OPERATIONSFLOW / SCOPE BOUNDARY"
          Title="Prototype Scope"
          Subtitle="OperationsFlow is a local portfolio prototype with a production-shaped workflow foundation. It proves business workflow design, evidence traceability, reporting, and Microsoft 365 readiness without pretending the local demo is already a production deployment."
          BadgeText="Scope Defined"
          BadgeClass="of-badge of-badge-warning">
    <Actions>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/integration-overview">Integration Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/reviewer-checklist">Reviewer Checklist</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-primary" href="/business-value">Business Value</a>
    </Actions>
</PageHero>

<PurposeNote Title="Purpose" Icon="🎯">
    <p>
        This page draws the line between what the Week 3 prototype proves locally and what still belongs to Week 4 production implementation.
        That makes the portfolio stronger because it is honest about the boundary instead of overclaiming.
    </p>
</PurposeNote>

<MetricGrid>
    <MetricCard Title="Week 3 Scope"
                Value="Local Foundation"
                Detail="Evidence workflow, document library, quality checks, reports, and activity traceability."
                Icon="✅"
                Tone="success" />

    <MetricCard Title="Week 4 Scope"
                Value="Production Layer"
                Detail="SharePoint, Entra ID, provider swap, permissions, and deployment readiness."
                Icon="🚀"
                Tone="warning" />

    <MetricCard Title="Current Storage"
                Value="Local"
                Detail="Files under wwwroot/uploads with metadata stored in SQLite."
                Icon="📁"
                Tone="info" />

    <MetricCard Title="Production Claim"
                Value="Not Yet"
                Detail="No fake claims about live Graph, tenant auth, or production deployment."
                Icon="⚠️"
                Tone="default" />
</MetricGrid>

<InfoPanel Title="Scope summary"
           Subtitle="The current prototype is valuable because it proves the workflow before production infrastructure is added."
           Tone="default">

    <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">In Scope</span>
            <h3>Week 3 local foundation</h3>
            <p>
                Local workflow capture, evidence uploads, document library, activity traceability, data quality, and reporting.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Planned</span>
            <h3>Week 4 production layer</h3>
            <p>
                SharePoint storage, Entra authentication, role enforcement, tenant configuration, and deployment readiness.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Not claimed</span>
            <h3>Live production deployment</h3>
            <p>
                The current app is not yet a live production system with real users, production backups, retention, or compliance sign-off.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Portfolio value</span>
            <h3>Production-shaped prototype</h3>
            <p>
                The project demonstrates how a local proof can be designed with a realistic Microsoft 365 production path.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</InfoPanel>

<TableCard Title="What the prototype currently proves"
           Subtitle="OperationsFlow proves more than CRUD screens. It shows an operational workflow loop with evidence and review.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Area</th>
                <th>Current proof</th>
                <th>Why it matters</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Workflow capture</span></td>
                <td>Work Orders, Corrective Actions, Document Intake, Risk, Training, Controlled Documents, and compliance pages.</td>
                <td>Shows how scattered operational work can be structured into reviewable records.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Ownership</span></td>
                <td>Owners, statuses, priorities, due dates, workload views, reminders, and management reports.</td>
                <td>Shows practical follow-up control instead of relying on memory, inboxes, or spreadsheets.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Evidence</span></td>
                <td>Record-level attachment panels across Work Orders, Corrective Actions, and Document Intake.</td>
                <td>Shows how proof, supporting documents, screenshots, PDFs, photos, and admin files can be linked to work records.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Document visibility</span></td>
                <td>Document Library reads active attachment metadata across modules.</td>
                <td>Gives reviewers a central place to see evidence instead of opening every individual record.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Traceability</span></td>
                <td>Activity Log records workflow and evidence actions.</td>
                <td>Shows who did what, what changed, and where review evidence exists.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Data quality</span></td>
                <td>Missing evidence checks for important overdue/high/needs-review records.</td>
                <td>Shows the system can identify weak records, not just display dashboards.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Reporting</span></td>
                <td>Evidence coverage and missing evidence reporting.</td>
                <td>Gives managers a clear review surface for operational completeness.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Production direction</span></td>
                <td>Technical, integration, role, audit, deployment, testing, and implementation overview pages.</td>
                <td>Shows the project has a realistic path from prototype to Microsoft 365 production implementation.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<div class="of-two-column-grid">
    <InfoPanel Title="Explicitly in scope for Week 3"
               Subtitle="These pieces are part of the local production foundation."
               Tone="success">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Persistence:</strong><span>Local SQLite foundation and migrations.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Metadata:</strong><span>DocumentAttachment model and service layer.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Storage:</strong><span>Local file upload provider.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Attachments:</strong><span>RecordAttachments component.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Records:</strong><span>Attachment panels on Work Orders, Corrective Actions, and Document Intake.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Library:</strong><span>Document Library across modules.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Registers:</strong><span>File counts on workflow register pages.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Traceability:</strong><span>Activity Log upload/delete events.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Quality:</strong><span>Data Quality missing evidence checks.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Reports:</strong><span>Evidence coverage and missing evidence reports.</span></li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>

    <InfoPanel Title="Explicitly out of scope until Week 4"
               Subtitle="These are production implementation tasks, not Week 3 local proof tasks."
               Tone="warning">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Graph upload:</strong><span>Real Microsoft Graph file upload.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>SharePoint:</strong><span>Real SharePoint document library storage.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Login:</strong><span>Microsoft Entra ID authentication.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Authorization:</strong><span>Role-based policy enforcement.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Tenant:</strong><span>Production tenant setup.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Secrets:</strong><span>Production secrets or certificate management.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Compliance:</strong><span>Retention policy and compliance sign-off.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Deployment:</strong><span>Hosted deployment with backup/restore plan.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Notifications:</strong><span>Live Teams/Outlook notification workflows.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Power BI:</strong><span>Production dataset/report deployment.</span></li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>
</div>

<GuidanceNote Title="Honest boundary" Icon="⚠️" Tone="warning">
    <p>
        Week 3 is not pretending to be final production. It proves the workflow and architecture foundation locally.
        Week 4 is where the production provider, identity, permissions, configuration, and deployment readiness should be added.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>